      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "From 1911 until the late 1920s, Gilbert earned the nickname “Hay Capital of the World” for its booming agricultural output.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gilbert%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Gilbert Elementary School, built in 1913, now houses the Gilbert Historical Museum, preserving the town’s early history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
